  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PERFORMANCE-BASED PARTNERSHIP SCHEME FOCUSING ON QUALITY PROGRAMMING, UNDERSTANDING CHANGE AND RESULTS FOR POOR HOUSEHOLDS AND COMMUNITIES</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This emergency food aid response aimed to meet the basic needs of people displaced by armed conflict in the Eastern region of Burkina Faso and was initiated in response to the immediate humanitarian needs of newly displaced households following confflict in the local area. . Marker 2.1 was selected because the primary objective of the response was to reduce the impact of the displacement of women, men, girls and boys linked to armed conflict in their villages of origin and who have restricted access to livelihoods and sectoral vulnerability, through the distribution of food kits to displaced households and awareness-raising on food and nutrition practices.</narrative>
  </description>
